        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-head);">
          <strong>What is a Specialized Investment Fund (SIF)?</strong><br />
          A <strong>Specialized Investment Fund (SIF)</strong> is a SEBI-regulated investment vehicle introduced as a bridge between Mutual Funds and Alternative Investment Funds (AIFs) / Portfolio Management Services (PMS). With a <strong>minimum investment threshold of ₹10 Lakhs</strong> per investor, SIFs allow Asset Management Companies (AMCs) to deploy sophisticated investment strategies—including Long-Short equity derivatives, downside inverse hedging, factor-based quant models, and structured debt—under the transparent framework of a mutual fund trust.
        </p>
